      hint: "Apply the formulas from slide 53. An absent key forces a full scan.",
      solution: "Best case: 1 comparison (the first position).\nWorst case: 1,000 comparisons (the last position).\nAverage case: (n + 1)/2 = 1,001/2 = 500.5 comparisons.\n\nIf the key is absent, the search must inspect all n elements, so the cost is the worst case: 1,000 comparisons. The average formula above assumes the key is present and equally likely to occupy any position."
